2026-09-08T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2240) '**Stem parity.** A sidecar shares its asset's stem exactly and adds `.xmp`. Nothing else names a sidecar, and `CITATION.xmp` is the one file named for the record rather than for an asset.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2240) '**Precedence.** The `.cff` is the authority and every `.xmp` is derived from it, so a disagreement is a stale derivation and not a decision to be made. An SVG may carry its packet inline for standalone rendering, and the sidecar still wins at ingest, so one reader does not see one story and another a different one. A `.lot` never carries RDF: a Lottie player wants strictly formed JSON, and the sidecar is mandatory there for that reason. A CineForm file is left alone. Its extended metadata resolves through the sidecar.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2240) 'The mapping, CFF 1.2.0 to ISO 16684-1
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2240) 'Namespaces: `dc:` Dublin Core, `xmp:` XMP Basic, `xmpRights:` Rights Management, `prism:` PRISM Basic, `xmpDM:` Dynamic Media, and `cff:` for the two fields no standard namespace carries.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2240) '| CFF field | XMP property | RDF structure |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2240) '| --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `cff-version` | `cff:schemaVersion` | plain literal |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `title` | `dc:title` | `rdf:Alt` with `xml:lang="x-default"` |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `message` or `abstract` | `dc:description` | `rdf:Alt` with `xml:lang="x-default"` |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `version` | `prism:version` and `xmp:Identifier` | plain literal |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `date-released` | `xmp:CreateDate` and `dc:date` | `rdf:Seq` |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `authors` | `dc:creator` | `rdf:Seq`, order preserved |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `license` | `dc:rights` and `xmpRights:Marked` | `rdf:Alt`, and `True` |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `doi` | `prism:doi` and `dc:identifier` | plain literal, `doi:` prefixed |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `repository-code` or `url` | `prism:url` and `dc:relation` | plain literal |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `keywords` | `dc:subject` | `rdf:Bag` |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `commit` | `cff:commit` | plain literal |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2240) 'An author with `name` is taken as written. One with `given-names` and `family-names` is joined in that order. `dc:format` carries the asset's media type, which is `video/lottie+json` for a `.lot`, `image/svg+xml` for an `.svg`, and the container's type for a clip. A media sidecar adds `xmpDM:videoFrameRate` and `xmpDM:duration`, which is what lets a timeline marker and an animation agree on a frame.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2240) 'The packet is wrapped in the standard `xpacket` markers so a reader that scans a file for one finds it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2240) 'Where this differs from the specification as it arrived
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2240) 'Two differences, both because an existing decision already carries an argument.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2240) '**The container is Matroska, not QuickTime.** The specification wraps CineForm in `.mov`. RFD66606-1123 chose Matroska and recorded why: AVI's 32-bit size field stops a file at 4 GiB, about 56 seconds of 4K60 at these bitrates, and MOV performed the same as Matroska while being less open. &{repo("interactor-cineform")} writes Matroska today, with a `V_MS/VFW/FOURCC` video track carrying `CFHD` and an uncompressed PCM audio track. A specification that named the container differently does not undo a measurement, so the container stays Matroska and the sidecar rule is unchanged: the stem is the stem whatever the extension.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2240) '**The converter is Elixir, not Python.** The workspace's rule is that new scripting is Elixir and that a reader parses rather than matches text. The specification's reference implementation builds RDF with an XML tree, which is the right shape; it is transcribed rather than adopted. A Python file that survives in this workspace is a runner wrapping a model and says so in its first line, which a metadata converter is not.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2240) 'What is built and what is not
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2240) 'Read on this desk, 2026-09-08:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2240) '| piece | state |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2240) '| --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `interactor-cineform` | source complete, **its own manifest root**; `contract-bus`, QCBOR, `cineform-sdk` and `libwebm` placed by it. Not compiled here |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `transport-cineform-tui` | source complete, a manifest root of its own, the job sender over the bus |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2240) '| `service-cineform` | composes the two so one `contract-bus` is checked out rather than two, and states which pin wins where they disagree |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2240) '| the engine-side writer | `modules/cineform` on the fork's `cineform-movie-writer` branch: `movie_writer_cineform.cpp`, `video_stream_cineform.cpp`, the class reference and a demo, with `thirdparty/cineform` and `thirdparty/libwebm` vendored on that branch. The branch is not merged into the working branch the manifest names |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2240) '| Lottie, written | already here and older than this document: `scripts/keypoint_render.py` writes an animation, `scripts/lottie.schema.json` is the 1.0 schema vendored with its provenance, and `scripts/check_lottie_spec.py` validates against it and caught 207 errors when first run |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2240) '| Lottie, read | ThorVG is vendored in the fork at `thirdparty/thorvg` with only the SVG and raster loaders; the loader sources are not in the placed tree, and a branch of the fork carries the re-vendoring unmerged. Upstream 1.0.3 is now placed at `2-contract/thorvg` with the loader intact |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2240) '| OpenColorIO | a build option of the OpenUSD source vendored under `datasource-flow`, not built here |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2240) '| cmake and ninja | **present and running**: cmake 4.4.3 and ninja 1.13.2 from the `datasource-flow` and `voxhammer.cpp` environments. Neither is on the default `PATH`, which is what an earlier reading of mine mistook for absence |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2240) '| FFmpeg | blocklisted, and now with the row that says so. Not installed and not on `PATH`, but two runnable copies sit in package caches; the one that runs is a GPL build and does hold a `cfhd` encoder, which is why the row argues licence rather than capability |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2240) 'Four of those rows correct an earlier claim of mine, and the pattern behind every one is the same: I probed a `PATH` or a single manifest and reported a filesystem fact. The engine-side writer is not an unplaced repository; RFD66606-1123 recorded that the separate repository was created, used and deleted and that the module shipped inside the fork, and the fork is placed. cmake and ninja run here. Lottie is not a new format for this workspace at all: a writer, a vendored schema and a validator predate this document, and this document's contribution is to say that the extension that validator already demands is the one the workspace uses.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2240) 'That gate had never run. Nothing invoked it, its `jsonschema` dependency was declared nowhere, and the writer kept emitting `.json` while the gate refused anything but `.lot`, so the rename it was written to force never happened. The dependency is pinned and the writer renamed in the same change as this document.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2240) 'The gates
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2240) '- `mix cff.xmp <in.cff> <out.xmp>` derives a sidecar; `--check` derives into memory and refuses when the file on disk differs, which is how a stale sidecar is caught rather than trusted.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2240) '- Every field in the matrix has a round-trip test: a record carrying it produces the property, and a record without it produces no empty element.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2240) '- Controls: a `.cff` that is not a mapping is refused by shape; an author with neither `name` nor `family-names` is refused with the entry named; a planted stale sidecar fails `--check`; a `.lot` carrying an RDF packet is refused; an asset with no sidecar is reported, counted and never skipped.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2240) '- The anti-entropy pass gains the pair "asset against its sidecar", with one planted sidecar-less asset reporting exactly one more.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2240) '- A clip's sidecar states the frame rate and duration, and the timeline marker that names the clip must agree; a planted disagreement fails.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2240) 'Static delivery
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2240) 'Deliverables ship as static files. The RFD site is one HTML page, its search index, its assets and an empty `.nojekyll`. The pages workflow runs `mix run scripts/pages_docs.exs --write` on each push to main and publishes `docs/`, and `docs/` is not committed (operator, 2026-11-24). MDEx turns the page's Markdown into HTML. The script's self-test checks that conversion. The edition line carries the newest author date among the page's own sources, and no commit name. `mix cff.xmp` reads the YAML subset the house records use and refuses the rest. Where the mapping offers two sources, `abstract` comes before `message` for `dc:description`, and a list of licences joins with " OR ".
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2240) '2351
 # tags: rebac:verbs-from
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2240) 'rfd-2240 provides cff-xmp-metadata-derivation
 # tags: rebac:relate
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2240) 'rfd-2240 spends elixir
 # tags: rebac:relate
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-09-08T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2240) 'rfd-2240 is_a workspace-policy
 # tags: rebac:relate
 Text:RFD2240  1 LINE
 Text:Written
